/- Classical provenance: Milne, Fields and Galois Theory v5.10, Theorem 5.30,
   Example 5.31(b), Remark 5.32. This supplies no arithmetic Frobenius or density
   theorem. The proof uses arbitrary finite prime supports and rational scalars;
   it is not a bounded enumeration, checker, numeric reduction or certified instance.
   The public prime-product obstruction is used by the simultaneous induction
   and the original GPC5 application. -/

